        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>You all know the one rule of PC ownership: If your PC glitches or isn\u2019t running at full efficiency, reboot it. But does that trick apply to your router, too?</p>\n\n\n\n<p>A <a href=\"https://www.bing.com/search?pglt=425&#038;q=rebooting+router+improve+bandwidth\">whole subset of the internet seems to think so</a>, including a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/explainlikeimfive/comments/20kjor/eli5_why_does_resetting_my_router_improve_my/\">Reddit thread on the subject</a>. But does it? According to my testing, there\u2019s anecdotal evidence to believe it does \u2014 and <em>aggregate</em> evidence that shows it doesn\u2019t do anything at all.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Granted, I don\u2019t own<em> your</em> router, so I can\u2019t predict the results of your setup. But anything that increases your router\u2019s throughput cuts down on download times, improving productivity and simply making your whole PC e",
